         `selftest` subcommand that demonstrates every lane can fire.
         WHAT THIS REPLACES, MEASURED 2026-07-28. ADR-0067 §9 phase 4 retired each receiver's second
         COMMITTED skill root; §8 forbids trading a loud failure for a quiet one, so all seven shipped
         a replacement alarm in their own retirement change. The result was seven implementations of
         ONE invariant — `scripts/check-skill-view-roots.sh` at 23,050 / 21,353 / 18,346 / 18,277 /
         14,864 bytes on SDD / Audio / Rendering / Game / Governance, `tests/composition/
         skill-view-roots.sh` on Net, `tests/composition/lib/skill-view-roots.sh` on Templates. A 55%
         size spread across files asserting the same thing, all written in one day, by a phase whose
         stated purpose is removing hand-copies. They were not a parallel MECHANISM — `skill-view` was
         already a kit-delivered source and `FsggKitCheckSkillView` already ran in every receiver —
         they were two lanes bolted onto it because `check` did not cover them. Now it does.
